  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>Six years under thirty kilometres of ice, four of them spent waiting on a ruling as to whether a working lamp constitutes a first-contact signal on a world where nothing has ever produced light. The ruling was that it does. The expedition is therefore the source of the register&#39;s largest body of recordings made in the dark, and of a method for describing a settlement you have never seen. Its budget was the smallest of any posting of its length and most of it went on batteries.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
